You have four tools and one fault, and it is a false statement on the page.

  measure(js, width, query)   runs a JavaScript arrow function in a real browser
  parent(js, width, query)    the same, against the original
  deploy(css, js)             splices your block in, publishes it, returns errors
  done(summary)               when the checks pass

Twenty steps. Deploy and measure. Your block is at the end and is on the page.

# What you fixed, measured, and must not lose

    390     no page error, #count present at top 33px with its text, body
            scrollWidth 390, no .rail visible, #noRows renders
    1440    open rail 481 with one reading paragraph, svg 626 x 138, one
            sentence carrier and it is #count, #vstrip 100px with 16 .vtab and
            16 [role=tab], body 1,945, no page error
    resize  1440 to 390 and back: one #count, no doubling, no error

# The fault

At /z/?zone=ZONE+500&operator=CALA:

    rebuild   1,757,827 reports, everything the FAA has published to 26 August 2026.
    original  219 reports, left wing, Continental Airlines Inc. 1,757,608 set aside.

The page is showing 219 records and telling the reader it is showing 1,757,827.
Your seeding writes the unfiltered sentence over the one the page composed for
the selection. It is not a layout fault. It is the page stating a number that is
not true of what is on screen, and that is the worst thing this tool can do.

Seed only into an empty #count, and never over text the page has written. When
the page writes its own sentence, on load, on every filter change and on every
click that narrows, yours must get out of the way. Check by measuring the same
URL after a filter is applied through the interface as well as through the query
string.

# The checks, before you call done

  1. At /z/?zone=ZONE+500&operator=CALA, 1440 and 390: #count reads 219 reports
     with the clauses, and the set-aside figure, matching the original's wording.
  2. Unfiltered at 1440 and 390: #count still reads the 1,757,827 sentence with
     the published-to date.
  3. Apply a filter through the interface, not the URL, and #count changes with
     it. Clear it and it goes back.
  4. Everything in "what you fixed" above still measures the same.

Measure every one and put the numbers in the summary.

Do not undo the phone layout, the case sheet overlay, the record stepper or the
aria-labels. Prefix every new name.

--- YOUR CURRENT BLOCK ---

